#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, liveness]
# doc: |
#   Static move-in-loop rejection (verdict = elaborate ∘ eval). `n` is declared in
#   an ENCLOSING scope, then moved by `consume(!n)` inside a 2-element `for` loop —
#   so the second iteration re-moves an already-moved place. The flow-sensitive
#   liveness gate rejects the move BEFORE eval with E_MoveInLoop — stdout stays
#   EXACTLY empty (the program never ran, which IS the verdict), exit 1. This is
#   the E_MoveInLoop sibling of reject_use_after_move.gg: it proves the MoveInLoop
#   code axis on all four lanes; flipping the expected `reject:` code must make
#   every lane MISMATCH (Core #6/#8). The 2-element iterable makes the re-move a
#   GENUINE multi-iteration reject (never a run-once loop).
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_MoveInLoop
#!end

void consume(String !s):
    pass

void main():
    String n = "outer"
    Vector[int] items = [1, 2]
    for i in items:
        consume(!n)
